From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG wifi: ath11k: optionally boot the firmware in resume instead of resume_early

Experiment for deep-sleep problem B (not for upstream): with
ath11k.debug_late_power_up=1 (kernel cmdline, or options ath11k ... in
modprobe.d; read-only at runtime) the default (non-WoW) PM policy skips
hif_power_up() in resume_early and does it at the start of the normal
resume callback instead. Wi-Fi still resumes (MHI channel devices are kept
across suspend, so QMI works inside the resume phase).

Question answered: does the phase in which the QCA6390 firmware is booted
after a CX collapse (early: cpuidle paused, most devices still suspended)
create the state that blocks later CX collapses? If CXSD repeats with the
knob, the cause is the phase/ordering; if not, it is something the kept
driver objects or the firmware boot itself leave behind.

Independent of 0121 (applies with or without it).
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -1284,6 +1284,15 @@
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(ath11k_core_suspend_late);
 
+/* DEBUG (q706f deep sleep, problem B): boot the firmware in the normal
+ * resume phase instead of resume_early, to test whether the phase in which
+ * the firmware boots after a SoC CX collapse matters. Not for upstream.
+ */
+static bool ath11k_debug_late_power_up;
+module_param_named(debug_late_power_up, ath11k_debug_late_power_up, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(debug_late_power_up,
+		 "DEBUG: power the target up in resume instead of resume_early (default: false)");
+
 int ath11k_core_resume_early(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 {
 	int ret;
@@ -1295,6 +1304,11 @@
 	if (ab->actual_pm_policy == ATH11K_PM_WOW)
 		return 0;
 
+	if (ath11k_debug_late_power_up) {
+		ath11k_info(ab, "debug: firmware power-up deferred to resume\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	reinit_completion(&ab->restart_completed);
 	ret = ath11k_hif_power_up(ab);
 	if (ret)
@@ -1379,6 +1393,15 @@
 	if (ab->actual_pm_policy == ATH11K_PM_WOW)
 		return ath11k_core_resume_wow(ab);
 
+	if (ath11k_debug_late_power_up) {
+		reinit_completion(&ab->restart_completed);
+		ret = ath11k_hif_power_up(ab);
+		if (ret) {
+			ath11k_warn(ab, "failed to power up hif during resume: %d\n", ret);
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
 	return ath11k_core_resume_default(ab);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(ath11k_core_resume);
